ocuments/s75951/annual-report-on-the-treasury-management-service-and-actual.pdf","committee":"Council","date":"02/07/2026","key":true},{"title":"Un-audited statement of accounts and AGS 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75844/un-audited-statement-of-accounts-and-ags-2025-26.pdf","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","date":"18/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix A for Un-audited statement of accounts and AGS 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75845/appendix-a-for-un-audited-statement-of-accounts-and-ags-2025.pdf","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","date":"18/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Appendix B for Un-audited statement of accounts and AGS 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75846/appendix-b-for-un-audited-statement-of-accounts-and-ags-2025.pdf","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","date":"18/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Annual report on the Treasury Management service and actual Prudential Indicators 2025-26","url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75847/annual-report-on-the-treasury-management-service-and-actual.pdf","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","date":"18/06/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-09","committee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-16","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"10.00 am","status":"Cancelled","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-27","committee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Commission","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Governance and Audit Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Capital programme delivered at only 83% with \u00a32.1m carried forward to next year","lead":"Capital delivery shortfalls can indicate slippage in project delivery capability or changes in priorities; \u00a32.1m carried forward is material and indicates potential delays in schemes expected to deliver benefits.","iso":"2026-07-02","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council tax collection ended below budget due to VOA delays, reduced new homes, and cost of living impacts","lead":"Council tax is the primary revenue source; under-collection signals both external pressures (development slowdown) and resident payment difficulty, both of which reduce revenue security for the council and increase default risk.","iso":"2026-07-02","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"A budgeting error within the PFI scheme resulted in the budget being set incorrectly for the year","lead":"PFI schemes are long-term contractual commitments with fixed costs; budgeting errors on these indicate control weaknesses in how major spending lines are forecast and monitored.","iso":"2026-07-02","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-07-02","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","headline":"Capital programme delivered at only 83% with \u00a32.1m carried forward to next year","detail":"Breckland spent only 83% of its planned capital budget in 2025-26, with \u00a32.1m of capital funding carried forward to 2026-27. The reasons for individual projects' underperformance are detailed in Appendix B but not in this summary.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital delivery shortfalls can indicate slippage in project delivery capability or changes in priorities; \u00a32.1m carried forward is material and indicates potential delays in schemes expected to deliver benefits.","figures":"\u00a32.1m carried forward; 83% spend rate","quote":"The capital programme was 83% spent against budget, with requests to carry forward \u00a32.1m of unused capital funding.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-02","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","headline":"Council tax collection ended below budget due to VOA delays, reduced new homes, and cost of living impacts","detail":"Council tax collection in 2025-26 was under budget. Three factors contributed: delays in the Valuation Office Agency rating new properties, a smaller than anticipated increase in new homes, and cost of living impacts affecting residents' ability to pay.","category":"income","matters":"Council tax is the primary revenue source; under-collection signals both external pressures (development slowdown) and resident payment difficulty, both of which reduce revenue security for the council and increase default risk.","figures":"Collection ended 'under budget' but no specific shortfall figure provided","quote":"Council Tax collection remains under budget for the year due to a range of reasons including delays in the VOA rating new properties, reduced increase in new homes and the cost of living impacts.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-02","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","headline":"A budgeting error within the PFI scheme resulted in the budget being set incorrectly for the year","detail":"The council made an error in calculating the budget for a PFI (Private Finance Initiative) scheme for 2025-26, which led to above-budget spend. No detail is provided on the scale of the error, which PFI scheme was affected, or how the error was discovered.","category":"governance","matters":"PFI schemes are long-term contractual commitments with fixed costs; budgeting errors on these indicate control weaknesses in how major spending lines are forecast and monitored.","figures":"No specific figure for the error disclosed; details are in Appendix A","quote":"A budgeting error within the PFI scheme resulted in the budget being set incorrectly for the year","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-02","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Financial Performance 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75947/75947.pdf","headline":"Bad debt and loan impairments for Breckland Bridge led to large above-budget spend","detail":"The council made a significant provision for bad debt and possible loan impairments related to Breckland Bridge during 2025-26, listed as a major area of above-budget spend. The report does not detail what Breckland Bridge is, the scale of the impairment, or whether further provisions may be needed.","category":"other","matters":"Loan impairments indicate that previous lending or investment decisions are underperforming, directly affecting cash reserves and raising questions about investment governance and whether future cash flows are at risk.","figures":"Described as 'large overspend' but no specific figure disclosed in this document; details are in Appendix A","quote":"A provision for bad debt and a provision for possible loan impairments for Breckland Bridge have led to a large overspend in this financial year","material":true},{"iso":"2026-07-02","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Annual report on the Treasury Management service and actual Prudential Indicators 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.breckland.gov.uk/documents/s75951/75951.pdf","headline":"Economic forecast inverted mid-year: rate cuts anticipated in strategy became rate rises expected by March 2026, driven by inflation and Middle East conflict.","detail":"The council's treasury strategy (approved December 2024) forecast gradual interest rate reductions through 2025-26. By April 2026, market expectations reversed to rate rises to 4\u20134.25% from 3.75%. The council cites Middle East conflict as driving inflation concerns, with CPI expected to breach 4.5% later in 2026. This materially raises future borrowing costs.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A rise in long-term borrowing rates (5-year PWLB now 4.50% vs 4.40% forecast) increases the cost of any future capital schemes and reduces the council's ability to afford them.","figures":"Bank Rate 3.75%; market now expects 4\u20134.25%; CPI forecast >4.5%","quote":"At the start of April 2026, the market expected Bank Rate to increase over the coming months to 4% or 4.25%, from 3.75%","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-02"},"name":"Breckland","findings_total":56,"news_drafts_total":3}}